  "live_records": {
    "q-103103": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103103",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The number of bacteria $y(t)$ in a culture after $t$ hours is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\ny=\\text{___}\\cdot {5}^{t}\n$$\n\nIf the culture started with $7$ bacteria and this number increases fivefold every hour, then what is the missing value in the expression for $y?$",
      "worked_solution": "The number of bacteria $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth factor of $5.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of the growth factor $b$) is\n\n$$\ny=a{b}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe have:\n\n- $a=7$ is the initial number of bacteria.\n\n- $b=5$ is the growth factor (the number of bacteria increases fivefold every hour).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in hours.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =7\\cdot {5}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $7.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
