    "q-61866": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61866",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "There are $14$ bacteria in a culture. Every minute, the number of bacteria increases by $15%.$ What function represents the number of bacteria $y(t)$ after $t$ minutes?",
      "worked_solution": "The number of bacteria $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $15%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe have:\n\n- $a=14$ is the initial number of bacteria.\n\n- $r=0.15$ is the growth rate ($15%$ expressed as a percent).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in minutes.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =14\\cdot (1+0.15)^{t} \\\\  & =14\\cdot {1.15}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
