    "q-61657": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61657",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A computer has $20$ files infected with a computer virus. The number of infected files $y(t)$ after $t$ days is given by the formula:\n\n$$\ny(t)=20\\cdot (\\text{___})^{t}\n$$\n\nIf the number of infected files increases $5%$ each day, then what is the missing value in the expression for $y?$",
      "worked_solution": "The number of infected files $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $5%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe have:\n\n- $a=20$ is the initial number of infected files.\n\n- $r=0.05$ is the growth rate ($5%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in days.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =20\\cdot (1+0.05)^{t} \\\\  & =20\\cdot (1.05)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $1.05.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
